d"]},"descriptions":{"english":["with a duck pond, a cricket green and a rather grand church","where the summer fête is the event of the year","known for its thatched cottages and a long feud over the best marrow","with one pub, one shop and a bus twice a week","where the bell-ringers practise every Thursday","tucked into a fold of the hills, with a stream through the middle","famous for its well dressing each spring","where the vicar keeps bees in the churchyard","with a market cross and a war memorial on the green","known for its cheese, its orchards and its endless roadworks","where the post office is also the tearoom","with a ford that tourists insist on driving through","where the parish council has argued about the bins since 1987","set around a green with a maypole","where the hedges are higher than the houses","famous for its annual cheese-rolling race","with a windmill on the hill that still grinds flour","where every cottage has roses round the door","on the old coaching road, with an inn from the 1600s","with a stately home that opens for teas on Sundays","where the Women's Institute runs everything","known for its scarecrow festival every August","where the cows have right of way","with a shop run entirely by volunteers","tucked away at the end of a single-track lane","with a church spire you can see from three counties","where the morris dancers come out on May Day","famous for its packhorse bridge and its tea garden","where nothing much happens, and everyone likes it that way"],"fantasy":["where the adventurers' guild is one notice board outside the inn","guarded by a retired paladin and a very old dog","where goblins raid the turnip fields every autumn","built around a ruined wizard's tower","with a shrine to a forgotten harvest god","where the miller swears the old granary is haunted","known for halfling bakers and dwarven ironwork","where a dragon's skull hangs over the inn door","on the edge of a wood the locals will not enter after dark","with a h