igger than the church","where the manor court meets under the great oak","on the edge of the royal forest, where the deer belong to the king","held by an old knight who would rather be farming","famous for its Whitsun fair and its stubborn oxen","where the monks keep bees for the abbey's candles","with a chapel built after a miracle at the ford","that has paid its dues in eels since before anyone can remember","where the lord's steward counts every egg","on a hill above the marsh, safe from the floods","with a market cross where the bailiff reads the king's proclamations","known for its cheesemakers and its quarrelsome priest","where the harvest is brought in by everyone at once"],"cosy":["with a tea shop, a bookshop and far too many cats","where everyone gathers on the green for the harvest supper","known for its jam, its honey and its very nosy neighbours","with a bakery that sells out of cinnamon buns by nine","where the hedgehogs have their own crossing","with a bridge over the brook and ducks to feed","where the post arrives by bicycle","famous for its pumpkin festival every autumn","where the library is a red telephone box","with a knitting circle that meets in the pub on Tuesdays","tucked between the hills, with apple trees in every garden","where nobody locks their door and the kettle is always on","with a little orchard and a pond full of frogs","known for its flower show and its fierce rivalry over sweet peas","where the first snowfall brings out every sledge in the county","with a cosy inn and a fire that never goes out","where the bees are as busy as the bakers","with a farm shop selling the best scones in the county","where the summer fair has a duck race on the stream","famous for its bluebell woods in spring","with a teashop that serves cake for breakfast","where the choir goes carolling round the cottages each December","with a market on Saturdays and a picnic on Sundays","where the cats nap in the sunniest windows","known for its lantern walk on the longest night","with a mill pond for skating when the winter is cold enough","where the hedgerows are full of blackberries every September","with a hall that hosts a dance every Friday","where the baker, the postie and the mayor are the same person","tucked in a valley where the mist sits low each morning"]}}}